<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0c054ac00b50> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft removed an article that advised tourists to visit the Ottawa Food Bank on an empty stomach. The food bank, a real charitable organization that feeds struggling families." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6445" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0c7625b32a82> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Headed to Ottawa? Here's what you shouldn't miss! reads its title, written under the official byline of 'Microsoft Travel.'" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8088" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1d4f84b9eba7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"Microsoft Travel\" appears to be another production use of generative AI technology." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6445" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/365e741ca4dc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft AI suggests food bank as a “cannot miss” tourist spot in Canada" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6445" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/370ea43a7cdf> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[6444] Microsoft removed an article that advised tourists to visit the Ottawa Food Bank on an empty stomach, after facing ridicule about the company's reliance on artificial intelligence for news." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6444" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3a52fbf17368> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Each section in the article, bylined vaguely by “Microsoft Travel,” had a brief text description of what you can expect from the destination." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8091" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/432332e7b089> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "As explained in a statement to The Verge from Jeff Jones, a senior director at Microsoft:" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8091" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/455d40203bca> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In response to Marx's post, frequent LLM critic Emily Bender noted, \"I can't find anything on that page that marks it overtly as AI-generated. Seems like a major failing on two of their 'Responsible AI' principles.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6445" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/458062140e35> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "We reported in 2020 about Microsoft laying off journalists at Microsoft News and MSN to replace them with artificial intelligence. However, the company says its content is not generated by the AI we're now used to in the form of large language models powering tools like the Bing chatbot or ChatGPT." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8091" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/463bc40bf229> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft lists Ottawa Food Bank as tourist destination, says 'human', not AI error" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6446" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4701ef2f4e68> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft's entire AI-generated catalogue should be suspect, as it's been remorselessly churning out AI-generated articles ever since it fired dozens of its journalists and editors at MSN in 2020." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8088" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4b748fa38922> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "CNET issued corrections on dozens of AI-written stories." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8091" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4e0eb0b33267> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft pulls article recommending Ottawa Food Bank to tourists" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6444" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5b3f962d41c2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft lists Ottawa Food Bank as tourist destination, says ‘human’, not AI error" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6446" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5eefe3e079b8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft removed an article that advised tourists to visit the Ottawa Food Bank on an empty stomach." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6444" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7fdeead8a84f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "However, the author of the Insider piece, Nathan McAlone, questioned the \"human review\" part, noting that Microsoft Travel also published a string of other travel articles with incongruous or nonsensical elements (all of which have now been taken down) that suggest largely algorithmic composition at work." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6445" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8acae7515c4b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft says listing the Ottawa Food Bank as a tourist destination wasn’t the result of ‘unsupervised AI’" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8091" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a6d87cc1952f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft Deletes Bizarre AI-Generated Travel Guide That Recommended Visiting Food Bank With an \"Empty Stomach\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8088" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a93a94805781> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“Every day our algorithms comb through hundreds of thousands of pieces of content sent by our partners,” Microsoft writes in the “About Us” page for its Microsoft Start program." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8091" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b48a106220fc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[6445] Late last week, MSN.com's Microsoft Travel section posted an AI-generated article about the \"cannot miss\" attractions of Ottawa that includes the Ottawa Food Bank" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6445" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/d0dd2c29b440> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[6445] Late last week, MSN.com's Microsoft Travel section posted an AI-generated article about the \"cannot miss\" attractions of Ottawa that includes the Ottawa Food Bank" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6445" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/da338fbc9934> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“Needless to say, this is not the type of messaging or ‘story’ we would ever put out or wish to be included in,” Samantha Koziara, communications manager at the Ottawa Food Bank, said in a statement to The Verge on Thursday." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8091" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dd2ef50d0fef> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The ‘human oversight’ curating algorithmic content on MSN somehow missed a list of tourist hot spots that put the food bank at number three." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8091" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e4cc34226b7e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The article was not published by an unsupervised AI. We combine the power of technology with the experience of content editors to surface stories. In this case, the content was generated through a combination of algorithmic techniques with human review, not a large language model or AI system." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6445" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f436ec6e6965> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "An AI-written article from Gizmodo failed to correctly list Star Wars movies in chronological order." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8091" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f85dd077519e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "BuzzFeed, like Microsoft, has used AI to write travel guides." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8091" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ff610dd3a0eb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The ‘human oversight’ curating algorithmic content on MSN somehow missed a list of tourist hot spots that put the food bank at number three." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8091" .

