<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/63d18a7eb714> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "For the food bank, Microsoft's summary included an astoundingly awful statement given the context of the place it was talking about: 'People who come to us have jobs and families to support, as well as expenses to pay. Life is already difficult enough. Consider going into it on an empty stomach." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6446" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6bbca9da4a63> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft removed an article that advised tourists to visit the Ottawa Food Bank on an empty stomach, after facing ridicule about the company's reliance on artificial intelligence for news." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6444" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/82b224fb7594> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Late last week, MSN.com's Microsoft Travel section posted an AI-generated article about the \"cannot miss\" attractions of Ottawa that includes the Ottawa Food Bank, a real charitable organization that feeds struggling families." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6445" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a3462dd4987f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In its recommendation text, Microsoft's AI model wrote, \"Consider going into it on an empty stomach.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6445" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cd1776783589> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Understandably, the Ottawa Food Bank was upset by its inclusion in a bubbly travel piece." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8088" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/085571fa7c29> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Bing, Bard, and ChatGPT: How AI is rewriting the internet" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8091" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e0291e35a21f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "We reported in 2020 about Microsoft laying off journalists at Microsoft News and MSN to replace them with artificial intelligence. However, the company says its content is not generated by the AI we’re now used to in the form of large language models powering tools like the Bing chatbot or ChatGPT." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8091" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/49c693f252ea> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "For the food bank, Microsoft's summary included an astoundingly awful statement given the context of the place it was talking about: 'People who come to us have jobs and families to support, as well as expenses to pay. Life is already difficult enough. Consider going into it on an empty stomach." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6446" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5b3cda30a57e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Understandably, the Ottawa Food Bank was upset by its inclusion in a bubbly travel piece." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8088" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7f243ada5b0c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Microsoft's entire AI-generated catalogue should be suspect, as it's been remorselessly churning out AI-generated articles ever since it fired dozens of its journalists and editors at MSN in 2020." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8088" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8d722114cf19> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Samantha Koziara, communications manager at the Ottawa Food Bank, told The Verge in a statement." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "8088" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ca336f2904d2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "First noticed by tech author Paris Marx on Bluesky, the post on the Ottawa Food Bank began to gain traction on social media late Thursday." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6445" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dd6600c72bf4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Verge had reported that the Microsoft listing for tourists had a food bank as the No 3 recommendation." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6446" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fa090dc639e9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Bender also pointed toward Microsoft policies; one is \"Transparency,\" and reads, \"How might people misunderstand, misuse, or incorrectly estimate the capabilities of the system?\"",
        "Bender also pointed toward Microsoft policies; one is \"Transparency,\" and reads, \"How might people misunderstand, misuse, or incorrectly estimate the capabilities of the system?\" and the other is \"Accountability,\" which states, \"How can we create oversight so that humans can be accountable and in control?\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6445" .

